    "body": "**Hub run (PathPilot Hub, 8L SIM, PathPilot v2.14.4), on this branch's goldens @ 4f72eaf4:**\n\n| Program | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `axial_drill_inch.nc` | ran to the end, 23 s, no alarm |\n| `axial_drill_mm.nc` | ran to the end, 27 s, no alarm |\n| `turning_inch.nc` | ran to the end, 41 s (262 lines), no alarm. Backplot: finish Ø0.276 (Ø7 mm) at the shoulder from Ø0.559 stock, 1.614 long, so the control-point fix (#630) holds |\n| `thread_g33_inch.nc` | ran to the end, 7 s, no alarm |\n| `thread_g76_inch.nc` | ran to the end, 4 s: `G76 ... R1 Q0 H0` without D accepted |\n| `thread_g76_mm.nc` | ran to the end, 3 s: `G76 P2 Z8 I-0.1 J0.8 K2.4 R1 Q0 H0` from X12.1 Z14; backplot cuts Ø13.70 → Ø9.60 on the +X side, Z14 → Z8 under M3 |\n\nCheck list: 1 (G76 without D, Z14→Z8 under M3) ✓; 3 (G33 runs, one groove) ✓ by run, not inspected pass by pass; 4 (I/J/K sign on the 8L tool post) ✓ by backplot; 5 (Ø7 at the Z2 shoulder) ✓. **Not run:** 2 (LH under M4), because no LH golden exists; the 15L simulator.\n\nThe two P0s this was held on are fixed on main and in this branch: #629 (4b549027) and #630 (c7ab1602).\n\nFlagging ready after a quick pass: mergeable, targeted gate green at this head (lathe_post_tormach, lathe_post_tormach_thread, conformance, clippy).",
