    "body": "<!-- pr-reviewer: 4f72eaf4f4717c059fb951c3f849aad429f8c98f -->\n**Review (M5, high tier, independent of the author; the M3 wrote this post): no blockers. Labelled `merge-ready`, and it merges at the next cut as a `feat`.**\n\n**Read:** `assets/posts/tormach-lathe.cps` in full; the registration in `posting.rs` and `conformance.rs`; the post-options UI row.\n- **Refusals really block.** Every `msg()`/`refuse()` goes to `message()`. The engine returns those as warnings, and `posting.rs` turns any warning into \"post blocked\". So off-meridian moves, posed A/B/C, control comp, an out-of-range T word, over-max rpm, taps, back-bores, off-axis holes, a wrong-hand half-turn, a lead mismatch and an unstateable G76 all stop the post.\n- **G76:** I/J/K are diameters on the control's grid, built from whole grid counts. The root rounds outward (never past the minor diameter) and J rounds shallower. The hand is checked against the spindle (`spinRev`). Hub confirms the diameter reading: root Ø9.60 = 12.0 − 2.4.\n- **G33:** one K per thread, from the THREAD record's lead, never re-derived from rounded Z. A half-turn turning against the section's spindle is refused.\n- **G95:** F = mm/min ÷ rpm, refused without an rpm. G97 or G96 with D = the machine's max rpm. M4 is written only when the thread's hand needs it, with a note to the operator.\n- The #629 and #630 fixes are in the branch, and the Hub run matches them: right-hand under M3, and Ø7 at the shoulder.\n\n**Gate (my own run at this head):** quick tier green. App suites (564 s, including `lathe_post_tormach`, `lathe_post_tormach_thread` and `conformance`) and ui suites (49 s); 0 failed.\n\n**Hub:** 6 goldens ran clean on the 8L SIM (see the comment above).\n\n**Non-blocking, filed as #772:** `sCss` (SurfaceSpeed) is never reset at a section's end, here or in `fanuc-lathe.cps`. A CSS section followed by one with no SurfaceSpeed would keep G96, and on centre that runs at the D cap. It's latent today, because no app path writes `PARAM SurfaceSpeed`.\n",
